{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"title":"SubgraphView","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubgraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L26"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its edge mask would cost O(m).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with vertex holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps at construction."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SubgraphView","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"densely. Made by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"text":" (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"text":", JGraphT’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"text":", LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"text":", Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations":{"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph-implementations","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph Implementations"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/UndirectedEdges":{"kind":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Base"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"title":"SubgraphView.UndirectedEdges","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edges of an undirected "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubgraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its positions."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/undirectededges","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedEdges":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directededges","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Base"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SubgraphView.DirectedEdges","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","abstract":[{"text":"The edges of a directed ","type":"text"},{"code":"SubgraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions. Stepping from one to the next skips the dropped ones.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Kept apart","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"go forward.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{